;; openicc — ICC situations, seeded from the public record.
;;
;; EVERY entry here is :unverified-seed and NONE of it is publishable. Gate G2
;; refuses a finding that cites an unverified registry entry, and this file is
;; the reason that gate exists rather than being a formality: the figures below
;; came from secondary sources, one of which (the UNIC Japan page the owner
;; pointed at) is dated to 2016 and states 124 States Parties and 10 situations,
;; both of which have moved since.
;;
;; What a seed is for: it gives the examiner bot something to reconcile AGAINST.
;; Verification is `openicc.statute/verified?` flipping after a run has compared
;; an entry to icc-cpi.int. Nothing here may promote itself.
;;
;; Note on what these rows are. A situation is not an accusation. The ICC's own
;; framing is that a SITUATION is a set of circumstances the Prosecutor may
;; examine; individual criminal responsibility is a separate question decided
;; case by case, and openicc's own output never states it (gate G13).
;;
;; sources
;;   https://www.unic.or.jp/activities/international_law/icc/   (requesting source, stale)
;;   https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court_investigations
;;   https://legal.un.org/icc/statute/99_corr/cstatute.htm      (Statute text)
;; retrieved 2026-08-21

